    <bpmn:process id="W_W4810" name="W4810. Reactive Fault Triage, Field Repair &amp; Vendor Dispatch" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Platform fault alert (W4807); customer-reported fault; failed pickup
Frequency: Per fault
Volume: ~40–100 locker faults/month at scale (scales with network size)
Owner: Locker Program Manager / Facilities (VS-138) / IT (VS-27)
Participants: Locker technician, Vendor (W4794), Store Ops (VS-07), IT (VS-27), CX (VS-13)
Source: workflow W4810 — Reactive Fault Triage, Field Repair &amp; Vendor Dispatch</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4810_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4810_Lane1" name="Facilities">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4810_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4810_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4810_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4810_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4810_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4810_Start3" name="Platform fault alert (W4807); customer-reported fault; failed pickup">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4810_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4810_Task4" name="Triage the fault from platform data: classify…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Triage the fault from platform data: classify (lock/sensor/screen/reader/connectivity/refrigeration/security), severity (safety/security-critical vs degraded), and scope (single compartment/bank/site/network); safety/security faults → immediate response (W4811)
Responsible (R): Facilities / IT / Locker Program
Accountable (A): Locker Program Manager
Duration: Per fault</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4810_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4810_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4810_Task5" name="Dispatch repair: in-house technician for simple fixes…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Dispatch repair: in-house technician for simple fixes (lock/sensor/clean/restart) or vendor field service under SLA (W4794); manage spare-parts (VS-31), customer impact (re-route orders W4804, notify affected customers W4805), and the repair SLA
Responsible (R): Facilities / Vendor / Procurement / CX
Accountable (A): Locker Program Manager
Duration: Per fault</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4810_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4810_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4810_Task6" name="Restore, retest, and return to service: verify the fix end-to-end (pickup…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Restore, retest, and return to service: verify the fix end-to-end (pickup test), update the asset/fault record (VS-35/W4807), feed root-cause to PM/analytics (W4809/W4815), and escalate recurring manufacturer defects to vendor/warranty (W4794)
Responsible (R): Facilities / Locker Program
Accountable (A): Locker Program Manager
Duration: Per fault</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4810_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4810_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4810_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4810_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4810_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-724 (ensure controlled execution — Maintenance, Integration, Compliance &amp; Network Analytics (PA-164.3).) | - CTL-724: faults triaged &amp; dispatched per SLA; security faults responded immediately; fixes retested; root-cause fed to PM
Owner: Locker Program Manager / Facilities (VS-138) / IT (VS-27)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W4810_Assoc9" sourceRef="W4810_Annotation8" targetRef="W4810_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W4810_Flow10" sourceRef="W4810_Start3" targetRef="W4810_Task4" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W4810_Flow11" sourceRef="W4810_Task4" targetRef="W4810_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W4810_Flow12" sourceRef="W4810_Task5" targetRef="W4810_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W4810_Flow13" sourceRef="W4810_Task6" targetRef="W4810_End7" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W4810_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W4810_plane" bpmnElement="W_W4810">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W4810_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W4810_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="950" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
