    <bpmn:process id="W_W4813" name="W4813. Data Privacy &amp; Consent for Locker Customer/Recipient Data" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Network launch (privacy-by-design); DSAR; periodic privacy review (VS-91); breach
Frequency: Continuous + per DSAR + annual review
Volume: ~all locker transactions collect customer/recipient PII; ~DSARs per year
Owner: Locker Program Manager (joint with DPO VS-91)
Participants: DPO (VS-91), Cyber (VS-27.3), Legal (VS-100.3), TPRM (VS-161)
Source: workflow W4813 — Data Privacy &amp; Consent for Locker Customer/Recipient Data</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4813_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4813_Lane1" name="Privacy">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4813_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4813_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4813_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4813_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4813_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4813_Start3" name="Network launch (privacy-by-design); DSAR; periodic privacy review (VS-91); breach">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4813_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4813_Task4" name="Govern the personal data the locker program collects: customer/recipient…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Govern the personal data the locker program collects: customer/recipient identity, contact (app/SMS/email), access codes/biometrics if used, order/parcel data, camera footage (VS-23), and 3P-recipient data (W4799) — classify per VS-91, minimize collection, secure storage (VS-27.3), retention aligned to operational/legal need then purge (VS-88)
Responsible (R): Privacy / Cyber / Locker Program
Accountable (A): DPO / Locker Program Manager
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4813_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4813_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4813_Task5" name="Handle DSAR per RA 10173 (VS-91.2 W271): access, correction, erasure (where…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Handle DSAR per RA 10173 (VS-91.2 W271): access, correction, erasure (where legally permissible), objection; manage consent for camera/recording ( signage notice), 3P-recipient data sharing (W4799 DPA), and the do-not-track/opt-out; coordinate with the DPO
Responsible (R): Privacy / Locker Program / IT
Accountable (A): DPO
Duration: Per DSAR</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4813_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4813_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4813_Task6" name="Run the breach-response path if locker PII/access/camera data is compromised…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Run the breach-response path if locker PII/access/camera data is compromised (VS-91 breach, NPC 72-hour); DPIA for high-risk processing (biometrics, large-scale recipient data, 3P-sharing); annual privacy review with the DPO and Cyber (VS-27.3); manage the locker vendor as TPRM (VS-161)
Responsible (R): Privacy / Cyber / TPRM / DPO
Accountable (A): DPO / Locker Program Manager
Duration: On event + annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4813_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4813_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4813_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4813_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4813_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-724 (ensure controlled execution — Maintenance, Integration, Compliance &amp; Network Analytics (PA-164.3).) | - CTL-724: data minimized &amp; classified; camera/3P-sharing consent + DPA; secured (VS-27.3); retention per VS-88 then purge; DSAR handled (VS-91.2)
Owner: Locker Program Manager (joint with DPO VS-91)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
