    <bpmn:process id="W_W4814" name="W4814. Uptime/SLA Management, Availability Reporting &amp; Vendor Governance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Continuous SLA monitoring; monthly vendor review; SLA breach
Frequency: Continuous + monthly
Volume: 1 network SLA across all locker banks (uptime target ≥ 98%)
Owner: Locker Program Manager / IT (VS-27)
Participants: Locker vendor (W4794), IT (VS-27), Finance (VS-17), Legal (VS-100.3)
Source: workflow W4814 — Uptime/SLA Management, Availability Reporting &amp; Vendor Governance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4814_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4814_Lane1" name="IT">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4814_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4814_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4814_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4814_Lane2" name="Locker Program">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4814_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4814_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4814_Start4" name="Continuous SLA monitoring; monthly vendor review; SLA breach">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4814_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4814_Task5" name="Monitor uptime/SLA per the vendor contract (W4794) and internal targets…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monitor uptime/SLA per the vendor contract (W4794) and internal targets: per-bank and network availability, compartment fault rate, session-success (W4802), time-to-repair (W4810), and security-event rate (W4811); track against SLA thresholds via the platform (W4807)
Responsible (R): IT / Locker Program
Accountable (A): Locker Program Manager
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4814_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4814_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4814_Task6" name="Administer SLA penalties/credits and vendor governance: where the vendor…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Administer SLA penalties/credits and vendor governance: where the vendor underperforms, apply contractual credits/penalties (W4794), manage performance improvement plans, and escalate persistent underperformance to re-compete (W4794); reconcile with Finance
Responsible (R): Locker Program / Finance / Legal
Accountable (A): Locker Program Manager / Legal
Duration: Monthly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4814_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4814_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4814_Task7" name="Report availability internally (store ops, leadership) and publish locker…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Report availability internally (store ops, leadership) and publish locker availability to customers (app VS-75) so customers see live status before traveling; feed uptime to analytics (W4815) and the network-strategy review (W4793)
Responsible (R): IT / Locker Program / App team
Accountable (A): Locker Program Manager
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4814_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4814_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4814_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4814_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4814_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-95 (ensure locker network custody &amp; uptime.) | - CTL-724: uptime monitored vs SLA; penalties/credits administered; live availability published; performance feeds strategy
Owner: Locker Program Manager / IT (VS-27)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
