    <bpmn:process id="W_W4816" name="W4816. Go-Live Readiness, Site Acceptance &amp; Hypercare for New Locker Sites" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Commissioning complete (W4797); site about to go live
Frequency: Per site
Volume: ~each site at launch
Owner: Locker Program Manager / PMO (VS-112) / Store Ops (VS-07)
Participants: PMO (VS-112), Facilities (VS-138), IT (VS-27), OCM (VS-134), CX (VS-13)
Source: workflow W4816 — Go-Live Readiness, Site Acceptance &amp; Hypercare for New Locker Sites</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4816_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4816_Lane1" name="Locker Program">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4816_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4816_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4816_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4816_Lane2" name="OCM">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4816_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4816_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4816_Start4" name="Commissioning complete (W4797); site about to go live">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4816_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4816_Task5" name="Run the go-live readiness &amp; site-acceptance test (SAT): end-to-end test…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Run the go-live readiness &amp; site-acceptance test (SAT): end-to-end test (order→compartment→access-code→pickup→confirm→OMS/inventory update; returns; 3P; security/tamper; accessibility), integration health (W4807), signage/wayfinding (VS-14), and store-team readiness; obtain sign-off before public launch
Responsible (R): Locker Program / Facilities / IT / OCM
Accountable (A): Locker Program Manager
Duration: Per site</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4816_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4816_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4816_Task6" name="Train the store team (VS-134 OCM): staging/replenishment (W4801), assisting…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Train the store team (VS-134 OCM): staging/replenishment (W4801), assisting pickups/returns (W4805), exception handling (W4808), accessibility assistance (W4812), and security/fault escalation (W4810/W4811); brief on the customer journey and the cross-sell opportunity
Responsible (R): OCM / Store Ops / Locker Program
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Per site</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4816_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4816_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4816_Task7" name="Enter hypercare: intensified monitoring (uptime, faults, session-success…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Enter hypercare: intensified monitoring (uptime, faults, session-success, pickup-success) for the first weeks, rapid-issue resolution with the vendor, and transition to steady-state operations (W4809/W4810) once stable; capture lessons for the next site (VS-133)
Responsible (R): Locker Program / IT / Vendor
Accountable (A): Locker Program Manager
Duration: Per site</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4816_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4816_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4816_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4816_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4816_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-724 (ensure controlled execution — Maintenance, Integration, Compliance &amp; Network Analytics (PA-164.3).) | - CTL-724: SAT passed before public launch; store team trained (VS-134); hypercare exited only on stability criteria
Owner: Locker Program Manager / PMO (VS-112) / Store Ops (VS-07)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
